# Supply chain and checkout

- Unit types: `SINGLE` | `CASE` | `BUNDLE`. CASE expands with `unitsPerCase` (seed uses 12). BUNDLE expands via `BundleItem`.
- Deduct **FEFO** (earliest `ProductLot.expiryDate` first) on the tracked SINGLE (or bundle components). Record `LotDeduction` on the order item.
- `receiveLot` upserts lot number + expiry and increments `stockQuantity`.
- If Stripe is not configured, demo checkout may mark paid immediately. When Stripe Checkout exists: keep order `PENDING`, deduct and set `PAID` **only** in the webhook after `checkout.session.completed`.
- On deduction failure, mark the order `CANCELLED` — do not leave a paid order with undeducted stock.
- Award points only after a successful `PAID` order (`pointsFromCents`, then `tierFromBalance`).
- Do not decrement lots below zero. Throw `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` / `INSUFFICIENT_LOT_STOCK`.
- Pure allocation math lives in `src/lib/inventory-logic.ts` and must stay unit-tested.
